    "https://foundation.fhsu.edu/about/careers/": {
      "title": "Join Our Team",
      "description": "Careers - Fort Hays State University Foundation Ways to Give Give Now Give Online Phone or Mail Stock & Securities Give Over Time Recurring Gifts Pledge Gifts FHSU Faculty & Staff Plan Your Gift Charitable IRA Estate Plan Give Assets Impact Student Stories Donor Impact Campus Capital Projects About Staff News Contact Us Make A Gift Join Our Team Open Positions: Director of Development - College of Education and Tebo Library Posting Date: July 28, 2026 Build Relationships. Inspire Generosity. Transform Futures. Every great university has stories of lives changed through generosity. A scholarship that made college possible. A donor whose vision inspired innovation. Those stories begin with people who believe in connecting passion with purpose. The Fort Hays State University Foundation is seeking a Director of Development to build meaningful relationships with alumni, donors, and friends who want to shape the future of FHSU by investing in two of the university's most transformative areas – the College of Education and the newly renovated Tebo Library . Make an Impact This is more than a fundraising position. As a Director of Development, you'll help the College of Education and Tebo Library by connecting generous supporters with initiatives that align with their passions. Working alongside university leadership, faculty, and Foundation colleagues, you’ll help donors create new scholarships, support essential programs, or advance campus projects. Every conversation has the potential to make a difference, and you’ll see firsthand the tangible results of your work. What You’ll Do Success in this role is built on trust and connection where no two days look alike. One day you'll meet with alumni across Kansas, listening to stories of their time on campus and learning what inspires them to give. The next, you'll collaborate with campus partners to identify fundraising priorities and create ways for donors to make a lasting impact. If you enjoy engaging with people, thinking strategically, and helping others, you'll find this work both rewarding and fulfilling. Who We're Looking For You don't have to come from higher education fundraising to flourish here. If you've built trust, helped clients achieve goals, or connected people with opportunities – whether in business development, sales, financial planning, nonprofit leadership, healthcare, or another relationship-driven field – we'd love to talk with you. The ideal candidate is: Passionate about helping others make a difference. A strong communicator who builds trust naturally. Curious, strategic, and motivated by meaningful work. Comfortable engaging with a wide variety of people and perspectives. Organized and able to manage multiple priorities while maintaining attention to detail. Self-motivated, collaborative, and excited to represent Fort Hays State University. Join Us If you're energized by what you’ve read here, we encourage you to explore the full position description to learn more about the role and qualifications. Then take the next step toward a career with purpose, measurable results, and lasting significance. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants are encouraged to apply by August 31, 2026, for best consideration. Appointment Date: Start date will be determined after acceptance of an offer and background check clearance. Required Application Details We will require application materials to include a completed application , a cover letter introducing the candidate and highlighting their interest in the position, their qualifications, and an explanation as to why they are a good fit for the role and the organization, as well as a resume. References are not required at this time, but may be requested from candidates as the search progresses. Material should be submitted as one PDF to FoundationHR@fhsu.edu . Questions If you have questions regarding this role, please contact Laura Dougherty at ladougherty@fhsu.edu . *Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Because of the sensitive nature of FHSU Foundation business and the importance of our reputation with donors, the FHSU Foundation conducts a comprehensive review of all applicants. By submitting your application, you authorize us to conduct reference checks and a review of available public information. Employment is contingent upon background and reference checks that the FHSU Foundation finds acceptable.* Why Join the Fort Hays State University Foundation? You'll join a team that’s ambitious and committed to a shared goal of creating opportunities for students and strengthening one of Kansas' leading regional universities. We believe great employees deserve exceptional support. At the FHSU Foundation, we invest in our employees as much as our mission. We strive to build upon your strengths, provide options for professional growth, and foster a collaborative, welcoming workplace where everyone can contribute and thrive. That’s why we offer an outstanding benefits package and unique perks that set us apart: Competitive, market-leading compensation Company-paid health, dental, vision, and life insurance A 401(k) with an immediate 10% employer contribution Generous paid time off, wellness leave, holidays, and reduced summer hours Tuition assistance, professional development, and certification support An engaging workplace culture focused on collaboration, innovation, and employee engagement About Us The FHSU Foundation is an independent 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization that advances Fort Hays State University through private philanthropy. Since 1945, we've partnered with alumni, donors, corporations, and friends of the university to create scholarships, enhance academic programs, and expand opportunities that transform the lives of our students. FHSU Home FHSU Alumni Employee Access Board Access Campus Forms Tax ID: 48-6108086 Ways To Give I Fed The Tiger Annual Giving Leadership Giving Legacy Giving Impact Student Stories Donor Impact About News Staff Contact Board of Trustees Privacy Policy Financials Careers FAQ Make A Gift Fort Hays State University Foundation One Tiger Place, Hays, Kansas 67601 | 785-628-5620 Follow Follow Follow Follow"
    },
    "https://www.fhsu.edu/career/index": {
      "title": "Career Development",
      "description": "Career Development Skip to main content Cookies on this site We use cookie to improve your experience and analyze site traffice. Learn morw Accept Reject Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Visit Give Directory News About Academics Admissions Athletics International Online Apply Career Development Home Career Development Closer to the Job of Your Dreams Your college experience ultimately helps illuminate the path toward the job of your dreams and the career of a lifetime. Fort Hays State University past and present students alike have utilized our offered resources and network of connections to get ahead – and stay there. Advance Your Future Get Ready, Get Set Stay ahead of the work – and the competition – by preparing yourself with the necessary knowledge and tools that will help you excel. Resume & Cover Letter Assistance - Write a resume and cover letter with the help of Career Development to help you land the job interview that sets you up for your future. Interviewing - Develop your interview skills through mock interviews, our online video interview training software Big Interview , and sample interview questions so your practice can make perfect when the right opportunity comes. Networking - Create lines of communication within the job market and build a network of professionals who understand your search. Job Search Booklet – You don’t have to search alone. Take information with you on how best to dress, search for jobs, maintain a personal calendar, and get ahead in finding the right job. Events - Enhance your career readiness by attending career fairs and other events. Graduate School Resources - Thinking about graduate school? Learn more about writing personal statements and admissions information. Tailored for Tigers – This professional clothing closet is free of change to currently enrolled FHSU students who want to dress to impress for interviews, business presentations, career fairs, or other professional activities. Find an Internship or Job Fort Hays State University is here to help get you ready not only to graduate, but to pursue the career of your choice. Whether you are still registered and looking for an internship or part-time job or getting ready to graduate and pursue career opportunities, our vacancy listings can help you get ahead. Handshake - Explore full-time job and internship listings, resume referrals, alumni networking and on-campus interviewing opportunities. GoinGlobal – Get information for students and alumni looking to job search globally and internationally. Internships – Apply your classroom learning, explore career options, and gain relevant work experience through internship opportunities. Career Fairs - Meet a large variety of potential employers under one roof with information on potential jobs and internship opportunities. Menu Career Development About Us Students Undergraduate Students Online Students International Students Veteran Students Graduate Students Video Presentations Employers Post a Job/Internship Career Fairs On-Campus Recruiting On-Campus Internships Faculty Calendar of Events Handshake Student/Alumni Login Employer Login About Handshake Tailored for Tigers Career Exploration Overview Current Students Prospective Students What Can I Do With A Major In... Majors and Graduate Programs Fair Staff How to Reach Us Career Development Fort Hays State University 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601 Center for Student Success 142 Phone: 785-628-4260 Email: careers@fhsu.edu Hours: Monday - Friday: 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Online Careers Apply Request Info Visit Give Help & Concerns Accessibility Ideas to Improve Freedom of Expression 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601-4099 785-628-FHSU (3478) Â© 2026 Fort Hays State University. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.fhsu.edu/career/jft/index": {
      "title": "Jobs for Tigers",
      "description": "Jobs for Tigers Skip to main content Cookies on this site We use cookie to improve your experience and analyze site traffice. Learn morw Accept Reject Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Visit Give Directory News About Academics Admissions Athletics International Online Apply Jobs for Tigers Home Career Development Jobs for Tigers Part-time Jobs for Tigers Looking for a part-time, off-campus job while going to school? If so, check out Handshake and get help locating part-time and temporary employment in the Hays area. Login to your Handshake account with your Workday username and password. Once logged in, go to Jobs on the menu bar. Select Part-Time Job and type Hays, KS . If you would like to receive emails when new jobs are posted, you will need to create a search alert in Handshake. Creating a search alert is easy, just select the link on the right side of the Jobs page. Career Development has partnered with Handshake - a modern career development platform - to be your one-stop-shop for finding part-time jobs in the Hays area, as well as nationwide full-time and internship opportunities. As of May 14, 2018, part-time off campus Jobs for Tigers listings are posted through Handshake. *Handshake does not list jobs that are on-campus.* Please contact the Student Employment office, Picken Hall Room 207A to inquire about on-campus jobs. Fort Hays State University makes no representations or guarantees about positions listed by the Career Development office. FHSU is not responsible for safety, wages, working conditions, or other aspects of off-campus employment. It is the responsibility of the student to research the integrity of the organizations to which they are applying for any position with an organization or private party. Menu Career Development About Us Students Undergraduate Students Online Students International Students Veteran Students Graduate Students Video Presentations Employers Post a Job/Internship Career Fairs On-Campus Recruiting On-Campus Internships Faculty Calendar of Events Handshake Student/Alumni Login Employer Login About Handshake Tailored for Tigers Career Exploration Overview Current Students Prospective Students What Can I Do With A Major In... Majors and Graduate Programs Fair Staff How to Reach Us Career Development Fort Hays State University 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601 Center for Student Success 142 Phone: 785-628-4260 Email: careers@fhsu.edu Hours: Monday - Friday: 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Online Careers Apply Request Info Visit Give Help & Concerns Accessibility Ideas to Improve Freedom of Expression 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601-4099 785-628-FHSU (3478) Â© 2026 Fort Hays State University. All rights reserved."
